 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "URL rules are deferred on the bundle at definition time, then replayed onto the app at registration.\n\n1. **Definition time:** `Bundle.attach_route_rule` (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:413`) doesn't touch the app. It validates the endpoint and view names, then calls `self.record(lambda s: s.attach_route_rule(...))`. `Bundle.record` (`:224`) appends that callback to `self.deferred_functions`. The `@bundle.route` decorator goes through this path via `Scaffold.attach_route_rule` in `src/tessel/sansio/scaffold.py:376`.\n\n2. **Registration entry point:** `App.register_bundle` (`src/tessel/sansio/app.py:571`) just calls `bundle.register(self, options)`.\n\n3. **Replay:** `Bundle.register` (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:273`) does the following:\n   - Records the bundle in `app.bundles[name]`.\n   - Builds a `BundleSetupState` with `make_setup_state` (`:246`).\n   - Adds the static-file rule through `state.attach_route_rule` if the bundle has a static folder.\n   - Runs `for deferred in self.deferred_functions: deferred(state)` (`:334`).\n\n4. **Applying to the app:** `BundleSetupState.attach_route_rule` (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:87`) does the following:\n   - Joins `url_prefix` onto the rule.\n   - Sets the default `subdomain`.\n   - Merges `url_defaults`.\n   - Builds the endpoint as `{name_prefix}.{name}.{endpoint}`.\n   - Calls `self.app.attach_route_rule(...)`, which is `App.attach_route_rule` at `src/tessel/sansio/app.py:606` and creates the actual URL rule.\n\n`src/tessel/bundles.py` only defines a thin `Bundle(SansioBundle)` subclass and isn't involved in this flow.",
